# Steamworks: Save files and Steam Cloud

Keep saves in files under the engine's per-user folder (Application.persistentDataPath, user://, FPaths::ProjectSavedDir) so Steam Auto-Cloud can sync them on every OS. Not in the Windows registry (PlayerPrefs), not at hard-coded Windows paths, and not with BinaryFormatter.

## Progress is kept in PlayerPrefs (warning)

- Why: On Windows PlayerPrefs live in the registry, which Steam Auto-Cloud cannot sync.
- Fix: Save progress to files under Application.persistentDataPath (keep PlayerPrefs for settings only).
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/features/cloud

## Hard-coded Windows paths (warning)

- Why: Paths like C:\ or %APPDATA% break on Steam Deck, Linux and macOS and on other Windows setups.
- Fix: Build paths from the engine's per-user folder (Application.persistentDataPath, user://, FPaths).
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/features/cloud

## Saves use BinaryFormatter (warning)

- Why: BinaryFormatter is obsolete and unsafe; a tampered save file (e.g. shared through Steam Cloud) can run code.
- Fix: Save with JsonUtility, System.Text.Json or another plain serializer.
- Source: https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/standard/serialization/binaryformatter-security-guide

With the steamworks-mcp server connected, `check_code(path)` finds these problems in the whole project, with file and line (`check_code(path, rules=["steamworks-saves-cloud"])` for this group only).
